<section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-center"><h2>What Are Fan Sections?</h2></div><p class="fcx-lead">A fan section is part of an air handling or ventilation system that includes the fan and related components required to move air through the system. It can be integrated into an AHU, packaged HVAC equipment, or existing ventilation setup.</p><p class="fcx-lead">Fan sections help create a compact and organised airflow arrangement. The selection of the fan type depends on the required air volume, pressure, space, noise level, and application.</p><div class="fcx-cards fcx-cards--2"><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-fan"></i></span><h3>Plug Fans</h3><p>Plug fans are designed to integrate directly into ductwork or equipment. Their compact construction makes them appropriate for installations where available space is limited.</p><p>The Delhi range includes plug fan sections with 315 mm to 1600 mm sizes, capacity up to 1,30,000 CMH, and static pressure up to 40 mmWG. The fans are equipped with adjustable pitch impellers to suit different airflow requirements.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-fan"></i></span><h3>Mixed Flow Fans</h3><p>Mixed flow fans integrate features of axial and centrifugal fan designs. This allows them to provide a balance between airflow and pressure while maintaining a compact arrangement.</p><p>The mixed flow fan design uses a backward-curved impeller to support better performance and lower noise. The impeller is also designed with integration of an external rotor motor in mind. These fans may be used in washrooms, hotels, auditoriums, stations, supermarkets, airports, and other public areas.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>Key Features of Fan Sections</h2><p><b>Fan Sections in Delhi</b> can be configured according to the requirements of different HVAC and ventilation systems. Some essential features include:</p><ul class="fcx-checks"><li>Compact and practical construction</li><li>Plug fan and mixed flow fan options</li><li>Adjustable pitch impeller for plug fans</li><li>Backward-curved impeller for mixed flow fans</li><li>Suitable for AHU integration</li><li>Ready-to-install configurations</li><li>Different sizes and airflow capacities</li><li>Suitable for new installations and retrofits</li><li>Focus on airflow, pressure, noise, vibration, and efficiency</li><li>Suitable for commercial and industrial applications</li></ul><p>The fan sections are selected according to airflow, static pressure, and site conditions so that the system can be properly integrated into the overall HVAC system.</p></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>Technical Specifications</h2><div class="fcx-spec"><table class="fcx-table"><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Fan Section Types</th><td>Plug Fans &amp; Mixed Flow Fans</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Size Range</th><td>315 mm to 1600 mm</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Capacity</th><td>Up to 1,30,000 CMH</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Static Pressure</th><td>Up to 40 mmWG</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Plug Fan Impeller</th><td>Adjustable Pitch</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Mixed Flow Impeller</th><td>Backward Curved</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Installation</th><td>AHUs, HVAC Equipment &amp; Duct Systems</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Applications</th><td>Commercial &amp; Industrial Spaces</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="fcx-note"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-sliders"></i></span><div><p>The specific specifications and configuration depend on the requirements of the HVAC project. Airflow, static pressure, installation space, and application should be considered before the final selection.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-center"><h2>Applications of Fan Sections</h2></div><p class="fcx-lead">Industrial Fan Sections can be used in many commercial and industrial ventilation systems. Their compact design and flexible configurations make them appropriate for different types of air management requirements.</p><div class="fcx-cards fcx-cards--4"><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-box"></i></span><h3>Air Handling Units</h3><p>Fan sections may be integrated into AHUs to offer the specified air movement through the system. They can be selected according to the airflow and pressure requirements of the unit.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-temperature-half"></i></span><h3>HVAC Systems</h3><p>In industrial HVAC systems, fan sections help move conditioned air through ducts and other components. They can be used in new systems as well as replacement and retrofit projects.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-people-group"></i></span><h3>Public Buildings</h3><p>Mixed flow fan sections can be used in places such as hotels, auditoriums, railway stations, supermarkets, airports, washrooms, and other public areas.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-industry"></i></span><h3>Industrial Facilities</h3><p>Factories and industrial facilities often require continuous ventilation. Fan sections can be configured to support air movement, supply air, or exhaust requirements depending on the system design.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-duo"><div class="fcx-panel"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-fan"></i></span><h2>Benefits of Fan Sections</h2><p>Fan sections provide various practical advantages for HVAC and ventilation projects. Their ready-to-install design can simplify integration with air handling units and duct systems.</p><p>Another advantage is the availability of different fan configurations. Plug fans can provide a compact solution for system integration, while mixed flow fans can provide a balance of airflow and pressure.</p><p>The selection also can consider vital factors such as noise, vibration, durability, efficiency, safety, bulk, and weight. This makes it easier to develop a fan section according to the requirements of a specific installation.</p></div><div class="fcx-panel"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-fan"></i></span><h2>Fan Sections Suppliers in Delhi</h2><p>Choosing appropriate <b>Fan Sections Suppliers in Delhi</b> is important for projects where the fan section needs to integrate efficiently with existing or new HVAC equipment. The supplier should understand the specified airflow, static pressure, dimensions, and operating conditions.</p><p>For Delhi projects, fan sections are supplied for air handling units, existing AHU retrofits, and packaged HVAC equipment. The current product page states that units are selected according to airflow, static pressure, and site conditions, with technical sizing support available before ordering.</p></div><div class="fcx-panel" style="grid-column:1/-1"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-industry"></i></span><h2>Fan Sections Manufacturer in India</h2><p>A reliable <b>Fan Sections Manufacturer in India</b> must be capable of providing different configurations for commercial, industrial, and HVAC applications. Proper manufacturing and selection are critical because the fan section becomes a fundamental part of the whole air management system.</p><p>The production facility is located in Neemrana, Rajasthan, on the Delhi-Jaipur highway. This location gives convenient access for Delhi NCR projects, while completed units can also be dispatched to other parts of India.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>How to Select the Right Fan Section?</h2><p>Before selecting a fan section, consider the following factors:</p><ul class="fcx-checks fcx-checks--long"><li><b>Airflow requirement:</b> Determine how much air the system needs to move.</li><li><b>Static pressure:</b> Check the pressure required to overcome system resistance.</li><li><b>Available space:</b> Select an appropriate configuration according to the installation area.</li><li><b>Fan type:</b> Choose between plug fan and mixed flow fan based on the application.</li><li><b>Noise requirements:</b> Consider the suitable noise level, especially in public and commercial areas.</li><li><b>Vibration:</b> Proper fan selection supports stable operation.</li><li><b>Application:</b> Consider whether the fan section will be installed in an AHU, HVAC system, commercial facility, or public building.</li></ul><p>Correct sizing helps the fan section work efficiently with the entire ventilation system.</p></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-center"><h2>FAQs</h2></div><div class="fcx-faq"><details><summary>What are fan sections used for?</summary><p>Fan sections are used in AHUs, HVAC systems, packaged equipment, and ventilation systems to provide controlled air movement.</p></details><details><summary>What types of fan sections are available?</summary><p>The Delhi range includes Plug Fans and Mixed Flow Fans. Plug fans are designed for compact integration, while mixed flow fans combine axial and centrifugal characteristics.</p></details><details><summary>What is the size range of the plug fan sections?</summary><p>The listed size range is 315 mm to 1600 mm, with capacity up to 1,30,000 CMH and static pressure up to 40 mmWG.</p></details><details><summary>Where can mixed flow fan sections be used?</summary><p>Mixed flow fans may be used in washrooms, hotels, auditoriums, stations, supermarkets, airports, and other public areas. They can also be used for different HVAC and commercial applications.</p></details><details><summary>Are fan sections suitable for AHU retrofits?</summary><p>Yes. Fan sections may be used for existing AHU retrofits and new air handling and packaged HVAC equipment. The final configuration should be selected according to airflow, static pressure, dimensions, and location conditions.</p></details></div><div class="fcx-center" style="margin-top:26px"><a href="product.php" class="btn-cyber btn-cyber--primary fcx-btn" title="Fan Air India Products">Learn More <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i></a></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-cta"><h2>Conclusion</h2><p><b>Fan Sections Manufacturers in Delhi</b> offer practical airflow solutions for AHUs, HVAC systems, packaged systems, and commercial ventilation applications. With plug fan and mixed flow fan options, different sizes, adjustable pitch impellers, and configurations designed for airflow and pressure requirements, these systems can be adapted to different project needs.</p><p>FanAir India Pvt. Ltd. offers fan sections for Delhi and NCR projects, such as new HVAC installations and AHU retrofit requirements. The system is manufactured at its Neemrana facility and can be supplied to Delhi as well as other places across India.</p><a href="../contact.php" class="fcx-cta__btn" title="Contact Fan Air India">Contact Us <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i></a></div></div></section>
  </div>



